ProsperoSunshine: tell the platform whose input it passes on

The PS5 host gives each paired device the console profiles it may play as, and a device with its own profiles gets its
own keyboard and mouse, seated in the profile its controller plays as. The console's shared keyboard and mouse belong to
no profile the host chose: with more than one profile signed in, the console asks who uses them, and whoever answers
picks any profile. So the platform has to know whose keyboard and mouse input it gets.

passthrough_next_message() tells it through the new platf::set_input_owner, by the session's feedback queue (the one
platf::set_gamepad_owner was given), and clears it afterwards. Two kinds of input run later from the task pool, where no
owner would be set: the key repeat (repeat_key) and the delayed release of the left button after absolute mouse input.
They set the owner of the stream they belong to as well; the repeat holds the stream by a weak pointer and stops once it
is gone. Input passed on with no owner set is Sunshine releasing what a stream held: the PS5 platform lets it release
only, never press.

